*.lock
!requirements.lock

# models/ is tracked on purpose: the Docker image and the Render deploy serve
# the dashboard without running `cipherguard train` first.

# Only the lab captures written by `cipherguard lab` are tracked. Anything else
# in samples/ stays out: live_snapshot.pcap is real traffic from this machine,
# and samples/real/ belongs to the Wireshark project (see
# scripts/fetch-real-captures.sh).
samples/*.pcap
!samples/backbone.pcap
!samples/downgrade.pcap
!samples/hardened.pcap
!samples/legacy.pcap
!samples/pqc_declined.pcap
!samples/pqc_hybrid.pcap
!samples/transitional.pcap
samples/real/
docker/captures/*.pcap

# A scan of this machine's real Wi-Fi surroundings (scripts/sync_live_wifi.py)
*.local.json

# docs/ is the output of `cipherguard export-demo`. It is tracked so GitHub
# Pages can also deploy from the branch; the Pages workflow rebuilds it.
